{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>A square is made up of four smaller squares, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If each of the smaller squares has a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, what is the perimeter of the larger square?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The side length of a square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of its perimeter, so the side length of each of the smaller squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a362fa10faa97931e8ff98810664b37e349a1bd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p>Two squares make up the side length of the larger square, so the larger square must have a side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85fe503753dabb6e699e6882ca6e083d532ffca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{4} \\times 2 = \\frac{N}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>This then means that the perimeter of the large square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0ef1a880de0bedef57315e2108b89b683a47fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{2} \\times 4 = 2N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/05062f6ceb8864aa268c38aa05ea3aa93ed2e83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. This means the perimeter would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206862010d7a24267c74552622ab7362565254b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 18 = \\boxed{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1\">Relay C Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Relay C Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a